# Regression test output (generated, not committed)
FlashIDA/test-output/
CLAUDE.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local Docker CI (docker/, ./ci) -- byproducts of running CI's own steps here.
#
# The runner deletes the strays below in its `finally`, so in a healthy run
# these lines never fire. They are belt-and-braces for the run that is killed
# half way: a dirty `git status` has to keep MEANING something, because the last
# and only unbypassable layer of the golden-write control is an unconditional
# `git status --porcelain` assertion. Five untracked files nobody ever cleans up
# is exactly how an operator learns to scroll past that signal.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# nunit3-console --result=<name>, run with CWD = repo root
# (.github/workflows/flashida-ci.yml:372 and :402 -- reproduced verbatim locally).
# TestResults.filtered.xml is the container's: a filtered "ci cs <filter>" run
# writes there deliberately, where the bridge-smoke gate cannot read it.
/TestResults.xml
/TestResults.filtered.xml
/RegenResults.xml

# FlashIDA/test-scripts/regression-runner.ps1:23-31 copies these three out of
# test-data/configs into the CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY, so the C++ engine can
# resolve the bare filenames in a method config. CWD is the repo root.
/test_inclusion_list.txt
/test_fasta.fasta
/test_target_log.log

# Container run output: logs, golden-capture staging, doctor reports, parser
# self-test output -- anything `ci` writes at the repo root.
/.container-out/
/flci-*.xml

# ccache and other build caches, for the case where one is pointed at the tree
# instead of at a Docker named volume (flashida-ccache-linux / -msvc).
/.ccache/
/ccache/

# A mis-pointed `cmake -B` at the parent root. The sanctioned build trees are
# OpenMS/cmake-build-{linux,msvc}-{release,debug}, already ignored inside the
# OpenMS submodule; nothing should ever configure a build tree up here.
/cmake-build-*/

# `Flash.exe` creates ONE TIMESTAMPED RUN FOLDER PER INVOCATION in its process
# CWD, and CWD for a container regression run is the repo root. runtime.log_dir
# is empty in all 41 committed configs and LogPathResolver.Compose treats empty
# as "." -- pinned by Flash.Tests.LogPathResolverTests
# .Compose_EmptyLogDir_UsesCurrentDirectory -- so each of the 14 cases in
# regression-runner.ps1 drops a yyyy-MM-dd-HH-mm-ss/ directory here holding the
# five engine streams plus a copy of method.json. Fourteen untracked directories
# per regression run is a larger dirty-status source than the five stray files
# above, and matters for the same reason. Anchored and directory-only; the
# trailing `*` catches the `_2` suffix Compose adds on a same-second collision.
/20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]*/
